#NOTE: SOMETIMES IT IS A BAD IDEA TO TRUNCATE HERE. IF YOU MERGE % is LOW OR YOUR NON-CHIMERIC % is LOW, CONSIDER ADJUSTING YOUR PARAMETERS FOR TRIMMING IN BOTH CUTADAPT AND DADA.

#trun-len-f will truncate the forward sequence after the # of basepairs you list
#trun-len-f will truncate the reverse sequence after the # of basepairs you list
#demux_seqs.qza is a zip file with each read which allows us to keep track of which read belongs to which sample after denoising.
#dada2_table.qza will output - sample ids and # of sample features but no interest in sequences
#dada2_rep_set.qza - has sequences, output of amplicon seq variants and all of the corrected seq are given a # called a hash, and whenever the same seq are found, it produces the same hash so easier to refer to same sequences by hash instead of referring to them by their entire name. 
#dada2_stats.qza - Denoising stats, tells us how the denoising step went.

Run the command:

qiime dada2 denoise-paired \
  --i-demultiplexed-seqs ./trimmed-demux.qza \
  --p-trunc-len-f 0 \
  --p-trunc-len-r 0 \
  --p-n-threads 6 \
  --o-table ./table.qza \
  --o-representative-sequences ./rep_set.qza \
  --o-denoising-stats ./stats.qza \
  --o-base-transition-stats base-transition-stats.qza


